sentences.l:
‘Zeus-sprung son of Laertes, many-devising Odysseus,
let no longing for a guide be a care to you beside the ship,
but having set up the mast and spread the white sails,
sit;

There into Acheron both Pyriphlegethon flow
and Cocytus, which is an offshoot of the water of the Styx,
and a rock, and the meeting of two loud-echoing rivers;

meanwhile then, having gone off, Circe, by the black ship
a ram had bound, a sheep, and a female, black,
easily having passed by;
